# Leave VITE_SCANNER_API_URL empty for local dev: the Vite server proxies
# the backend paths (vite.config.ts), so the app works locally and through
# the share link without needing this set.
#
# PRODUCTION (Vercel): Vite's dev proxy does not exist in a static build, so
# this MUST be set to your deployed backend's full URL, e.g.
#   VITE_SCANNER_API_URL=https://your-service.onrender.com
# Set it as an environment variable in the Vercel project settings, not in
# a committed file. Never put secrets (OPENAI_API_KEY etc.) in a VITE_*
# variable -- anything prefixed VITE_ is bundled into the client-side
# JavaScript and is visible to anyone who opens the site.
VITE_SCANNER_API_URL=
# Where Vite forwards those paths locally. Must match SCANNER_PORT in
# backend/.env. Not used in production (VITE_SCANNER_API_URL replaces it).
SCANNER_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5050
